title: 'C-c o l : skg-paste-link'
pid: 4cd48bf1-ddc3-4e2f-852e-89d07d831792
body: |2-
  Inserts, at the cursor, a link to the node
  whose ID is at the top of the linkstack.
  Does not modify the stack.

  It asks for the link's label, starting from the node's title.
  In that prompt, shift-left and shift-right show the tree above or
  below in the stack instead, cycling; the tree shown when you press
  RET is the one pasted. A chain (see skg-push-ancestry) pastes as
  links joined by its edges, and the prompt shows all of it but the
  last label, which is the only one you can edit.
  In the minibuffer it asks nothing, and pastes the top tree.
